## Write down a, b and c and the formula
Here $a = -1$, $b = 6$, $c = -4$.
x &= \frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}
&= \frac{-6 \pm \sqrt{6^2 - 4(-1)(-4)}}{2(-1)}
## Simplify the square root
&= \frac{-6 \pm \sqrt{36 - 16}}{-2}
&= \frac{-6 \pm \sqrt{20}}{-2}
&= \frac{-6 \pm 2\sqrt{5}}{-2}
&= 3 \mp \sqrt{5}
## Find both solutions
x &= 3 + \sqrt{5} = 5.2360\ldots
x &= 3 - \sqrt{5} = 0.7639\ldots
## Round to one decimal place
x &= 5.2
x &= 0.8
ANSWER: x = 5.2 \text{ or } x = 0.8

## Find the modulus of z_1 and z_2
|z_1| &= \sqrt{3^2 + 1^2}
&= \sqrt{10}
$|z_2| = \sqrt{3^2+(-1)^2} = \sqrt{10}$ as well.
## Find the distance between z_1 and z_2
$z_1 = (3, 1)$ and $z_2 = (3, -1)$.
|z_1 - z_2| &= \sqrt{(3-3)^2 + (1-(-1))^2}
&= \sqrt{0 + 4}
&= 2
## Use the cosine rule in the triangle with sides $|z_1|$, $|z_2|$ and 2
The side opposite $\theta$ is 2, so $\cos\theta = \dfrac{|z_1|^2 + |z_2|^2 - 2^2}{2|z_1||z_2|}$.
\cos\theta &= \frac{10 + 10 - 4}{2\sqrt{10}\sqrt{10}}
&= \frac{16}{20}
&= 0.8
ANSWER: \cos\theta = 0.8

## Name the curve
A quantity that is multiplied by the same factor (0.8) every year follows an exponential curve.
ANSWER: \text{Exponential}

## Choose 3 of the 6 boxes
The order does not matter, only which 3 boxes are chosen.
\binom{6}{3} &= \frac{6!}{3!\,3!}
&= \frac{6 \times 5 \times 4}{3 \times 2 \times 1}
&= \frac{120}{6}
&= 20
ANSWER: 20

## Find the radius
The radius is the distance from the centre $(-4, 3)$ to the point $(3, 4)$.
r &= \sqrt{(3-(-4))^2 + (4-3)^2}
&= \sqrt{7^2 + 1^2}
&= \sqrt{49 + 1}
&= \sqrt{50}
## Write the equation of the circle
(x-h)^2 + (y-k)^2 &= r^2
(x+4)^2 + (y-3)^2 &= (\sqrt{50})^2
(x+4)^2 + (y-3)^2 &= 50
ANSWER: (x+4)^2 + (y-3)^2 = 50
